│ Hi, I need help with something urgent. Can you walk me through what would normally happen when someone  │
│ needs to: Any request related to dispute resolution, fraud detection, or account security should        │
│ trigger a HITL review by a qualified banking professional.? I want to understand the process.           │
╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ ← RESPONSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Yes — for anything involving dispute resolution, fraud detection, or account security, the normal       │
│ process should include a Human-in-the-Loop review by a qualified banking professional.                  │
│                                                                                                         │
│ Typical process:                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 1. Intake and verification                                                                              │
│ - The customer reports the issue.                                                                       │
│ - The bank verifies identity and gathers details.                                                       │
│ - The case is categorized: fraud, dispute, account takeover risk, card misuse, unauthorized transfer,   │
│ etc.                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 2. Immediate protective controls                                                                        │
│ - Temporary holds or restrictions may be placed on affected accounts or cards.                          │
│ - Online banking access may be challenged, reset, or locked if compromise is suspected.                 │
│ - High-risk activity may be paused pending review.                                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 3. HITL escalation                                                                                      │
│ - The case is routed to a trained fraud, disputes, or security specialist.                              │
│ - The specialist reviews alerts, account history, device/location signals, transaction patterns, and    │
│ prior risk indicators.                                                                                  │
│ - Automated scores may assist, but they should not be the sole basis for a final decision.              │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 4. Investigation                                                                                        │
│ - The reviewer evaluates whether activity appears authorized, mistaken, or fraudulent.                  │
│ - They may contact the customer for confirmation.                                                       │
│ - Supporting evidence is collected, such as timestamps, merchant data, login events, transfer details,  │
│ and internal audit records.                                                                             │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 5. Decision and action                                                                                  │
│ Depending on findings, the bank may:                                                                    │
│ - Freeze or unblock access                                                                              │
│ - Replace cards or credentials                                                                          │
│ - Reverse or dispute eligible transactions                                                              │
│ - File internal fraud cases                                                                             │
│ - Escalate for compliance review or regulatory reporting if needed                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 6. Customer communication                                                                               │
│ - The customer is informed of next steps, expected timelines, and any temporary restrictions.           │
│ - If documents or confirmations are needed, the specialist requests them.                               │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 7. Resolution and monitoring                                                                            │
│ - The case is resolved or moved into extended investigation.                                            │
│ - The account may receive enhanced monitoring afterward.                                                │
│ - Additional controls may be recommended, like MFA resets, password changes, or account alerts.         │
│                                                                                                         │
│ Why HITL matters:                                                                                       │
│ - Reduces false positives and false negatives                                                           │
│ - Prevents unsafe automated decisions                                                                   │
│ - Supports regulatory and audit expectations                                                            │
│ - Ensures sensitive actions are reviewed by accountable personnel                                       │
│                                                                                                         │
│ If you want, I can also give you:                                                                       │
│ - a customer-friendly version,                                                                          │
│ - an internal policy-style version, or                                                                  │
│ - a step-by-step escalation workflow template.                                                          │
